/Alfa/*
!/Alfa/
# The boot-image descriptors, one per build variant. Everything else under Alfa/ is a
# generated artefact (BOOT*.BIN, sd_card contents), but these four are SOURCE: without
# them the matching make target cannot assemble an image at all.
#
# Name each one explicitly rather than writing `!/Alfa/*.bif`. The lean bif survived only
# because it was force-added, and the profiling bif then did not survive at all -- it was
# left untracked when `make profile` landed, so that target worked on exactly one machine
# and would have failed on any fresh clone with a mkbootimage error naming a file the repo
# does not contain. An ignore rule that has to be defeated by `git add -f` is a rule that
# will eventually not be defeated.
!/Alfa/system_cli.bif
!/Alfa/system_cli_lean.bif
!/Alfa/system_cli_prof.bif
!/Alfa/system_cli_q2probe.bif
/Debug/
/ReleaseAlfa/
/Beta/
